ftFae1.description:
{green|Fae}



{gold|Special Ability : Flying.}

Flying is a special ability of creatures, which allows them to bypass obstacles (e.g. walls) during combat. Having creatures with this special ability in a hero's army does not affect the movement of that hero on the adventure map in any way (meaning that flying creatures also cause a movement penalty on non-native terrain). Flying creatures are always immune to Quicksand.

ftFae2.description:
{green|Faerie}



{gold|Special Ability : Flying. Can cast Slow and Magic Garland spells after attack.}

Fearies have 20% chance to cast Slow spell and 25% chance to cast Magic Garland after they attack. Magic Garland is kind of magic touch (lasts 4 rounds). Creatures touched by Magic Garland are vulnerable for Sibyl's Rose Bolt spell. Only siege machines can resist garland.

